    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Wherefore the noble soldier of Christ [Ignatius], being in fear for the Church of the Antiochians, was, in accordance with his own desire,",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "brought before Trajan, who was at that time staying at Antioch, but was in haste [to set forth] against Armenia and the Parthians.",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And when he was set before the emperor Trajan, [that prince] said unto him, “Who art thou, wicked wretch,",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "who settest thyself to transgress our commands, and persuadest others to do the same, so that they should miserably perish?”",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Ignatius replied, “No one ought to call Theophorus wicked; for all evil spirits have departed from the servants of God.",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But if, because I am an enemy to these [spirits], you call me wicked in respect to them, I quite agree with you;",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s10",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for inasmuch as I have Christ the King of heaven [within me], I destroy all the devices of these [evil spirits].”",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s11",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Trajan answered, “And who is Theophorus?” Ignatius replied, “He who has Christ within his breast.”",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s12",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s12",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Trajan said, “Do we not then seem to you to have the gods in our mind, whose assistance we enjoy in fighting against our enemies?”",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s13",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s13",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Ignatius answered, “Thou art in error when thou callest the dæmons of the nations gods.",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s14",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s14",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For there is but one God, who made heaven, and earth, and the sea, and all that are in them; and one Jesus Christ, the only-begotten Son of God, whose kingdom may I enjoy.”",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s15",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s15",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Trajan said, “Do you mean Him who was crucified under Pontius Pilate?” Ignatius replied, “I mean Him who crucified my sin,",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s16",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s16",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "with him who was the inventor of it, and who has condemned [and cast down] all the deceit and malice of the devil under the feet of those who carry Him in their heart.”",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s17",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s17",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Trajan said, “Dost thou then carry within thee Him that was crucified?”",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s18",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s18",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Ignatius replied, “Truly so; for it is written, ‘I will dwell in them, and walk in them.’",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s19",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s19",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "” Then Trajan pronounced sentence as follows: “We command that Ignatius, who affirms that he carries about within him Him that was crucified,",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s20",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s20",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "be bound by soldiers, and carried to the great [city] Rome, there to be devoured by the beasts, for the gratification of the people.”",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s21",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s21",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "When the holy martyr heard this sentence, he cried out with joy, “I thank thee, O Lord,",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s22",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s22",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "that Thou hast vouchsafed to honour me with a perfect love towards Thee, and hast made me to be bound with iron chains, like Thy Apostle Paul.”",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s23",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s23",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Having spoken thus, he then, with delight, clasped the chains about him; and when he had first prayed for the Church, and commended it with tears to the Lord,",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.ii.s24",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.ii.s24",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "he was hurried away by the savage cruelty of the soldiers, like a distinguished ram the leader of a goodly flock, that he might be carried to Rome, there to furnish food to the bloodthirsty beasts.",
    "chunk_index": 30,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.iii.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.iii.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Wherefore, with great alacrity and joy, through his desire to suffer, he came down from Antioch to Seleucia, from which place he set sail.",
    "chunk_index": 31,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.iii.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.iii.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And after a great deal of suffering he came to Smyrna, where he disembarked with great joy, and hastened to see the holy Polycarp, [formerly] his fellow-disciple, and [now] bishop of Smyrna.",
    "chunk_index": 32,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.iii.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.iii.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For they had both, in old times, been disciples of St. John the Apostle.",
    "chunk_index": 33,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.iii.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.iii.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Being then brought to him, and having communicated to him some spiritual gifts, and glorying in his bonds, he entreated of him to labour along with him for the fulfilment of his desire;",
    "chunk_index": 34,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.iii.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.iii.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "earnestly indeed asking this of the whole Church (for the cities and Churches of Asia had welcomed the holy man through their bishops, and presbyters, and deacons, all hastening to meet him,",
