  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.vi.s11",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.vi.s11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For only the harder portions of his holy remains were left, which were conveyed to Antioch and wrapped in linen, as an inestimable treasure left to the holy Church by the grace which was in the martyr.",
    "chunk_index": 62,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.vii.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.vii.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Now these things took place on the thirteenth day before the Kalends of January, that is, on the twentieth of December, Sura and Senecio being then the consuls of the Romans for the second time.",
    "chunk_index": 63,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.vii.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.vii.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Having ourselves been eye-witnesses of these things, and having spent the whole night in tears within the house, and having entreated the Lord, with bended knees and much prayer,",
    "chunk_index": 64,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.vii.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.vii.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "that He would give us weak men full assurance respecting the things which were done, it came to pass, on our falling into a brief slumber, that some of us saw the blessed Ignatius suddenly standing by us and embracing us,",
    "chunk_index": 65,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
      350,
      500
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius#MartIgn.vii.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/martyrdom-of-ignatius",
    "canonical_ref": "MartIgn.vii.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "while others beheld him again praying for us, and others still saw him dropping with sweat, as if he had just come from his great labour, and standing by the Lord.",
    "chunk_index": 66,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 400,
    "date_range": [
